  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Tl;dr music is cool but is being used inconsistently and can be annoying in big lobbies. Adding: A specific music input channel that can be muted, volume controlled and bypass player proximity would help greatly. Also adding a player specific avatar volume slider/mute button for those who use the avatar sound system to play music.\nMe and my friends love to play music over our mics in vrchat. Its a good way to connect and have fun together but i often run into the problem of multiple people wanting to do the same thing. This often means that i refrain from playing my music as i dont want to contribute the the already crowded vc. Having a separate audio channel you can  send your music to so others can mute your music and not your voice would be very helpful in this regard. In a similar sense i have met multiple users that play music via the avatar sound channel. Mainly to make sure that the sound volume isnt proximity based. Adding a map wide music toggle would be great so the avatar system isnt being used for that and to make it toggle-able. Maybe a player specific avatar volume slider could be useful if its a specific person you wanna muse for music but not for voice.",
